Introduction to Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
What is RAG?

Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is an AI technique that improves the responses of Large Language Models (LLMs) by retrieving relevant information from external knowledge sources before generating an answer.

Instead of relying only on the knowledge stored during training, the model first searches for relevant documents and then uses those documents to generate a more accurate and up-to-date response.
